<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39570" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pūmĭcĕus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		pumex, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of pumice-stone</i>, or <i>of soft stone;</i> in
			gen. (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">molae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					6, 318</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sedes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					7, 419</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">antra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 3, 1, 144</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fontes,</span>”
				<i>flowing from pumice-stone</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					4, 57, 2</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oculi,</span>”
				<i>not in a condition to weep</i>, <i>stony</i>,
						<i>dry</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps. 1, 1, 73</span></i>
			.</div>
